# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MerrageHall — environment configuration
#
# THE ONLY CREDENTIAL THE APP NEEDS is the Postgres connection string.
# Get it from Supabase → Project Settings → Database → Connection string →
# "Transaction pooler" tab (port 6543):
#
#   DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres"
#
# ▸ Docker/Coolify: set it as an environment variable in the UI (recommended).
# ▸ Anywhere else: copy this file to .env, fill in DATABASE_URL, run.
#   The container's bootstrap script reads .env automatically.
# ▸ Special characters in the password (@ # ? / space) must be URL-encoded.
#
# NOT needed (Supabase SDK only — this app talks to Postgres directly):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres"

# Your app's public domain (venue subdomains become slug.<domain>).
# Set this when deploying so the homepage isn't mistaken for a venue domain.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ROOT_DOMAIN="marriagehall.digitalcomrade.in"

# Only for plain-HTTP deployments (no TLS). Leave unset on HTTPS.
# ALLOW_INSECURE_COOKIES="true"
